  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InteractableAsset
  asset:
    name: Roadblock
    explanation: This roadblock is managed by the local council to restrict access
      to unsafe or closed roads. The council is responsible for ensuring it is correctly
      positioned and maintained.
    councilOwned: 1
    category: Road Infrastructure
    description: A temporary road safety barrier used to block vehicle access and
      warn drivers of roadworks, hazards or closures.
    locationDescription: Positioned on a suburban road near an intersection, preventing
      vehicles from entering a restricted section of the street.
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    question: Who is responsible for maintaining this asset?
    realWorldPurpose: Roadblocks protect drivers, pedestrians and workers by restricting
      access to hazardous areas, construction zones and temporarily closed roads.
    responsibilityDetails: For council-managed road closures, the local council or
      its authorised contractors are responsible for installing, inspecting and removing
      roadblocks. Other road authorities may manage barriers on major roads.
    interestingFact: Roadblocks often feature reflective orange and white markings
      to make them more visible to drivers, particularly at night or in poor weather.
    interactionHint: Press the Interact key to inspect.
