    name: Public Fountain
    explanation: This fountain is a public asset maintained by the local council.
      The council is responsible for keeping it clean, safe and operational for the
      community.
    councilOwned: 1
    category: Parks & Recreation
    description: A decorative public fountain that circulates water and enhances
      the appearance of the surrounding neighbourhood.
    locationDescription: Located in a grassy public area beside the suburban footpaths,
      surrounded by residential houses and trees.
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    question: Who is responsible for maintaining this asset?
    realWorldPurpose: Public fountains improve the appearance of community spaces
      and create pleasant areas for residents and visitors to enjoy.
    responsibilityDetails: The local council is responsible for maintaining council-owned
      fountains, including cleaning, water quality management, pump repairs and ensuring
      the surrounding area remains safe.
    interestingFact: Many decorative fountains use recirculating pumps to reuse the
      same water, reducing the amount of fresh water needed to keep them running.
    interactionHint: Press the Interact key to inspect.
